<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-21262] kernel update [RHEL 9.8 5.14.0-687.66.1.el9_8]</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21262</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Security Fix(es):&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: net/smc: fix UAF in smc_cdc_rx_handler() by pinning the socket (CVE-2026-64541)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: sctp: avoid auth_enable sysctl UAF during netns teardown (CVE-2026-68162)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA AES cipher key requests (CVE-2026-68452)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: s390/zcrypt: Validate length for CCA ECC private key requests (CVE-2026-68451)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: sunrpc: pin svc_xprt across the asynchronous TLS handshake callback (CVE-2026-72222)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: sunrpc: wait for in-flight TLS handshake callback when cancel loses race (CVE-2026-72221)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: fs/resctrl: Fix use-after-free during unmount (CVE-2026-72080)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: sctp: keep chunk-&amp;gt;transport in step with the list it is queued on (CVE-2026-74588)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: sctp: clear new_transport when removing a peer (CVE-2026-74586)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: sctp: validate cookie AUTH state before use (CVE-2026-74752)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: s390/vfio_ccw: Cancel existing workqueues (CVE-2026-80553)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: powerpc/pseries: papr-phy-attest - validate cmd.length, plug mem leak (CVE-2026-80571)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: s390/qeth: validate user buffer length in SNMP and ARP query ioctls (CVE-2026-80584)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: sctp: stop processing a packet once its association is deleted (CVE-2026-89479)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: openvswitch: Fix CT limit teardown use-after-free (CVE-2026-89488)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;kernel: s390/boot: Avoid IPL parameter append past command line (CVE-2026-98403)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="https://access.redhat.com/errata/product/479/ver=/rhel---9/x86_64/RHSA-2026:95370" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://access.redhat.com/errata/product/479/ver=/rhel---9/x86_64/RHSA-2026:95370&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
